  "body": "This addresses https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6040\r\nThis is very similar to auto-expanding details elements: https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/6466\r\nHowever, this is a more generic version to provide the same functionality without the use of details elements.\r\nExplainer here: https://github.com/WICG/display-locking/blob/main/explainers/hidden-content-explainer.md\r\n\r\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\r\n   * Chrome\r\n   * https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/612\r\n   * https://lists.webkit.org/pipermail/webkit-dev/2022-March/032142.html\r\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\r\n   * find-in-page can't be tested in WPT: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/issues/29915\r\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/32465\r\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/33221\r\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\r\n   * Chrome: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1055002\r\n   * Firefox: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1761043\r\n   * Safari: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=238266\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\r\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\r\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\r\n\r\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\r\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\r\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\r\n    and remove what's below.\r\n-->\r\n***\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7475/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 16, 2022, 11:32 PM UTC (c885c5e)\">/browsing-the-web.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7475/755ae90...c885c5e/browsi